### Purpose

Docker-based launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents. Each persona ships its own `CLAUDE.md` and (optionally) `.conf`; all share OAuth credentials, workspace mapping, slash commands, status line, skills, and toolchain caches. Multiple persistent sessions per agent; prior conversations resume automatically. Per-agent filename *tags* + per-instance *modes* compose into a layered Docker image and per-launch behavior.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+ host launcher (walrus operator in expressions, frozen dataclasses, modern union types, `from __future__ import annotations`)
- `prompt_toolkit` (TUI picker), `python-dotenv` (`.conf` parsing), `rich` (markdown rendering for previews + F8 legend); stdlib `readline` for workspace tab-completion
- Docker + Compose v2; base is `debian:bookworm-slim` + Claude Code + jq/yq/fd/tree/ripgrep; `[code]` adds Rust/Node/uv + python3-dotenv, `{auto}` adds iptables + sudo + firewall script, `{DooD}` mounts host docker socket, `{web}` adds playwright CLI + chromium apt deps
- `unittest` test suite (500+ tests, ~0.3s); `mypy` + `ruff` as the dev-side check stack (no CI gate)

